/**
 * @defgroup RoModular_Governance_AIAgents AI Agent Guidance
 * @ingroup RoModular_Governance
 * @brief Provider-neutral instructions for AI-assisted work across RoModular repositories.
 *
 * @section RoModularAIAgentsPurpose Purpose
 *
 * RoModular uses a shared operating contract so AI coding agents receive the
 * same architectural boundaries, evidence requirements, and safety rules
 * regardless of whether the active runtime is Codex, Claude Code, or another
 * compatible tool.
 *
 * The shared documents describe desired behavior. They do not require a
 * particular model, vendor, or subagent implementation. A runtime may delegate
 * a role to an isolated subagent or perform that role in the current session.
 *
 * @section RoModularAIAgentsStructure Structure
 *
 * The RoModular repository contains the canonical shared guidance:
 *
 * @code{.text}
 * RoModular/
 * |-- AGENTS.md
 * `-- .romodular/
 *     |-- CONTRACT.md
 *     |-- roles/
 *     |   |-- architecture-auditor.md
 *     |   |-- documentation-curator.md
 *     |   |-- release-auditor.md
 *     |   `-- repository-maintainer.md
 *     `-- workflows/
 *         |-- release.md
 *         `-- repository-audit.md
 * @endcode
 *
 * `AGENTS.md` is intentionally a small router. The `.romodular/` directory is
 * the source of truth for shared policy, roles, and repeatable workflows.
 * Provider-specific files are added only when a provider requires behavior
 * that cannot be expressed by the shared entry point.
 *
 * @dot
 * digraph AgentGuidance {
 *     graph [bgcolor="transparent", rankdir=TB];
 *     node [shape=box, style="rounded"];
 *
 *     Repository [label="Repository\nAGENTS.md"];
 *     Contract [label="RoModular\nCONTRACT.md"];
 *     Roles [label="Bounded roles"];
 *     Workflows [label="Repeatable workflows"];
 *     Runtime [label="Codex / Claude /\ncompatible runtime"];
 *
 *     Runtime -> Repository [label="discovers"];
 *     Repository -> Contract [label="loads when available"];
 *     Contract -> Roles [label="constrains"];
 *     Contract -> Workflows [label="constrains"];
 * }
 * @enddot
 *
 * @section RoModularAIAgentsRepositoryAdapters Repository Adapters
 *
 * Every independently cloned repository needs a small root `AGENTS.md` because
 * repositories do not automatically inherit instructions from sibling Git
 * repositories. The adapter must:
 *
 * 1. Look for `../RoModular/.romodular/CONTRACT.md` and read it when available.
 * 2. Select the applicable shared role and workflow.
 * 3. Define only the repository-specific purpose, boundaries, supported
 *    commands, compatibility requirements, and validation rules.
 * 4. Provide a minimal local fallback when the RoModular sibling is absent.
 * 5. Report when shared guidance could not be loaded.
 *
 * The relative sibling path is a convenience for the standard local checkout:
 *
 * @code{.text}
 * GitHub/
 * |-- Foundation/
 * |-- MCC/
 * |-- MIDILAR/
 * |-- RoModular/
 * `-- RoModularBuild/
 * @endcode
 *
 * A standalone clone remains usable because its adapter contains the essential
 * local rules. Shared guidance never expands the repositories or actions that
 * the user placed in scope.
 *
 * @section RoModularAIAgentsRoles Roles
 *
 * | Role | Responsibility | Default authority |
 * | ---- | -------------- | ----------------- |
 * | Architecture Auditor | Repository ownership, dependency direction, and shared boundaries | Read-only |
 * | Repository Maintainer | Focused implementation and proportional validation | Changes requested by the user |
 * | Release Auditor | Version, CI, package, API, documentation, and release evidence | Read-only |
 * | Documentation Curator | Accuracy, navigation, status language, and rendered documentation | Documentation changes requested by the user |
 *
 * A role defines responsibility and expected evidence; it is not permission to
 * modify additional repositories, commit, push, tag, merge, publish, or release.
 * Those actions still require explicit user authorization.
 *
 * @section RoModularAIAgentsWorkflows Workflows
 *
 * The initial workflow set contains:
 *
 * - **Repository audit:** inspect repository state, declared contracts,
 *   implementation evidence, documentation claims, risks, and ordered next
 *   actions.
 * - **Release readiness:** verify versioning, API changes, tests, packages,
 *   documentation, CI, platform evidence, and hardware-validation boundaries
 *   before recommending whether a release is ready.
 *
 * Workflows complement each repository's checked-in scripts and presets. They
 * do not replace build, test, install, export, or release automation.
 *
 * Use @ref RoModular_Governance_AIAgents_Workspace to create a complete local
 * checkout and the workspace-level entry point consumed by compatible agents.
 *
 * @section RoModularAIAgentsAdoption Adoption Status
 *
 * | Repository | Root adapter | Shared-contract loading |
 * | ---------- | ------------ | ----------------------- |
 * | RoModular | Implemented | Owns the canonical contract |
 * | Foundation | Implemented | Loads the sibling contract conditionally |
 * | MusicCompositionCore | Implemented | Loads the sibling contract conditionally |
 * | MIDILAR | Planned | Pending repository reconstruction |
 * | RoModularBuild | Planned | Not yet integrated |
 *
 * This table describes instruction integration, not repository maturity. See
 * @ref RoModular_Governance_Status for the ecosystem status vocabulary.
 *
 * @section RoModularAIAgentsLimitations Limitations and Future Distribution
 *
 * The sibling lookup works well in the standard local workspace but cannot be
 * assumed in CI, cloud workspaces, or standalone clones. The local fallback is
 * therefore mandatory.
 *
 * A future portable RoModular agent package may distribute shared skills and
 * workflows to supported runtimes. Until that package has an installation,
 * versioning, and update policy, `.romodular/` remains the canonical source and
 * repository adapters remain deliberately small.
 */
